<title>AUSTRALIA: ICI Australia says foreign group could bid.</title>
<headline>ICI Australia says foreign group could bid.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemicals group ICI Australia said on Sunday it was possible a foreign company could bid for it after plans by its British parent Imperial Chemical Industries Plc to sell its 62.4 percent sometime in July.</p>
<p>ICI Australia managing director Warren Haynes said he expected foreign ownership of the company would be about 50 percent of the 62.4 percent stake ICI plc was putting on the market if a competitor does not buy the whole company.</p>
</text>
